# Commits listed here are skipped by `git blame` when
# `blame.ignoreRevsFile` is configured to point at this file
# (see CONTRIBUTING.md). Only mechanical, no-logic-change reformats
# belong here — never a commit that also changes behavior.
#
# An entry is added ONLY after its commit has landed on `main`, never for a
# PR that will be squash-merged: the squash rewrites the SHA into a new merge
# commit, so a pre-squash entry stops being an ancestor of `main` the moment
# it merges (#986, #1004). `bun run check:blame-ignore` enforces both halves
# — ancestry against `origin/main` and a mechanical (normalized-equal) diff
# — so an entry that fails either is rejected before it can rot silently.
